<title>USA: Beekeeper vote keeps honey checkoff program-USDA.</title>
<headline>Beekeeper vote keeps honey checkoff program-USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Honey producers and importers voted overwhelmingly to continue a program check-off program that encourages honey consumption, the U.S. Agriculture Department announced Tuesday.</p>
<p>Assessment is one cent per pound on honey produced domestically or imported.</p>
<p>USDA said 82 percent of the votes case in an August referendum were in favor of continuation of the program. A simple majority was needed.</p>
</text>
